      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks like it may be an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled daily dose of 2,550 mg for immediate-release metformin. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose, the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis and severe GI effects, is high even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me that and add a note about the rationale. I'd still want you to confirm it explicitly before I enter it."
      }
